You write a handy script, `greet.py`. Later a test file does `import greet` to reuse one helper — and the whole program runs, asking for input in the middle of your tests! The fix is a tiny, famous pattern. A file defines main(), keeps helpers importable, and calls main only under the conventional name guard, so tests can import it without running the command. In this lesson you'll write and run a saved script while explaining its top-level execution.

```predict
